<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 5 April, from 823 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rome" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">823 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,203 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Paschal I crowns Lothar co-emperor in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Easter Sunday Pope Paschal I crowned Lothar, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a>, as co-emperor in St Peter's. The ceremony reinforced the idea that imperial legitimacy came through papal coronation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1242">1242 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">784 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander Nevsky defeats the Teutonic Order on frozen Lake Peipus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Novgorod's forces under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> beat the Livonian branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-ice">Battle on the Ice</a>, halting the Order's eastward expansion into Russian lands.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1722">1722 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">304 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacob Roggeveen reaches Easter Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> navigator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacob-roggeveen">Jacob Roggeveen</a> became the first known European to reach <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Rapa Nui</a>, naming it after the day of his arrival, Easter Sunday. His crew recorded the island's great stone moai.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington issues the first presidential veto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington vetoed a bill apportioning seats in the House of Representatives, judging it unconstitutional. It was the first use of a power that later presidents would wield thousands of times.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1879">1879 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">147 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chile declares war on Peru and Bolivia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chile's declaration opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a>, fought over the nitrate-rich Atacama Desert. Victory gave Chile the coastal provinces and left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> without access to the sea.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1955">1955 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">71 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Winston Churchill resigns as Prime Minister</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aged 80 and in failing health, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> stepped down as Prime Minister and was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-eden">Anthony Eden</a>. It closed a career at the top of British politics spanning more than half a century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-eden">Anthony Eden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nirvana's Kurt Cobain dies in Seattle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Kurt Cobain, singer and guitarist of Nirvana, died at his Seattle home aged 27; his body was found three days later. His death closed the band that had carried grunge into the mainstream.</p></div></li></ol>
